# Non-Reproducing Brief Studio Lifecycle-Projection Timing Observation

During the first complete affected-suite rerun after the external power interruption, the existing Brief Studio imported-package scenario timed out while polling for the projected terminal state. Expected `latestBindingStatus: "TERMINATED"`; the last observed value was `"ATTACHED"`. The run result was 1 failed / 28 passed files and 1 failed / 126 passed tests.

The implementation diff does not touch the lifecycle observer/projection owner. The exact integration file was then rerun three consecutive times without any code or environment change; all three runs passed (3/3 tests each). The entire 29-file affected suite was subsequently rerun and passed (127/127 tests); that final suite evidence is in `04-affected-application-suites.log`. This observation is retained as a non-reproducing timing signal, not hidden or classified as a product defect.

